const llmActionsProps = {"enabled":true,"providers":["claude","chatgpt","perplexity","gemini"],"placement":"header","copyButton":true,"footerLink":true,"markdownBody":"# Stage 10: Keys {#stage-10-keys}\n\nDefine keys for the product name, version, download URL, and selected topics. A `\u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/>` uses text from a key definition; an `\u003cxref keyref=\"install\"/>` uses a key to identify a link target. Updating the definition changes each reference that resolves to it.\n\nStore product values in `keydefs-product.ditamap` and include that map with `\u003cmapref>`. Define topic keys with `@keys` on the guide's existing `\u003ctopicref>` elements.\n\n**Time:** about 30 minutes. **You need:** stage 09 complete.\n\nRecorded diagnostic examples below come from earlier runs. File counts, paths, and stage numbers can differ. Run the gate for your current checkout.\n\n## Step 1: Define the product keys {#step-1-define-the-product-keys}\n\n:::steps\n1. **Create `keydefs-product.ditamap`** in the project root.\n\n   ```xml {title=\"keydefs-product.ditamap\"}\n   \u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n   \u003c!DOCTYPE map PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Map//EN\" \"map.dtd\">\n\n   \u003cmap>\n     \u003ctitle>Product key definitions\u003c/title>\n\n     \u003ckeydef keys=\"product-name\">\n       \u003ctopicmeta>\n         \u003ckeywords>\n           \u003ckeyword>Audacity\u003c/keyword>\n         \u003c/keywords>\n       \u003c/topicmeta>\n     \u003c/keydef>\n     \u003ckeydef keys=\"product-version\">\n       \u003ctopicmeta>\n         \u003ckeywords>\n           \u003ckeyword>3.4\u003c/keyword>\n         \u003c/keywords>\n       \u003c/topicmeta>\n     \u003c/keydef>\n     \u003ckeydef keys=\"download-url\" href=\"https://www.audacityteam.org/download/\" scope=\"external\" format=\"html\">\n       \u003ctopicmeta>\n         \u003clinktext>the Audacity download page\u003c/linktext>\n       \u003c/topicmeta>\n     \u003c/keydef>\n     \u003ckeydef keys=\"project-extension\">\n       \u003ctopicmeta>\n         \u003ckeywords>\n           \u003ckeyword>.aup3\u003c/keyword>\n         \u003c/keywords>\n       \u003c/topicmeta>\n     \u003c/keydef>\n   \u003c/map>\n   ```\n2. **Read the elements**\n\n   - `\u003ckeydef>` is a `\u003ctopicref>` specialized for defining keys. `@keys` is the key name. A `\u003ckeydef>` with no `@href` defines text only.\n   - The text comes from `\u003ckeywords>` inside `\u003ctopicmeta>`: the `\u003ckeyword>` is what a `\u003ckeyword keyref>` in a topic renders as.\n   - `download-url` has an `@href` with `@scope=\"external\"` and `@format=\"html\"`, exactly as an external `\u003cxref>` in stage 07. Its `\u003clinktext>` is the text an empty `\u003cxref keyref=\"download-url\"/>` shows, because a web page has no DITA title to borrow.\n   - A keydef map is an ordinary map with a `\u003ctitle>`. It is never published on its own; the guide references it.\n:::\n\n## Step 2: Bring the keys into the guide and key the topics {#step-2-bring-the-keys-into-the-guide-and-key-the-topics}\n\n:::steps\n1. **Edit `audacity-guide.ditamap`**\n\n   ```diff {title=\"audacity-guide.ditamap\"}\n   --- a/audacity-guide.ditamap\n   +++ b/audacity-guide.ditamap\n   @@ -7,11 +7,14 @@\n        \u003cshortdesc>Record, edit and export audio with Audacity, from your first track to a finished file.\u003c/shortdesc>\n      \u003c/topicmeta>\n    \n   +  \u003cmapref href=\"keydefs-product.ditamap\"/>\n   +  \u003ckeydef keys=\"start-here\" href=\"topics/what-is-audacity.dita\"/>\n   +\n      \u003ctopichead navtitle=\"Getting started\">\n        \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/what-is-audacity.dita\" collection-type=\"family\">\n   -      \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\"/>\n   +      \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\" keys=\"digital-audio\"/>\n        \u003c/topicref>\n   -    \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/installing-audacity.dita\"/>\n   +    \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/installing-audacity.dita\" keys=\"install\"/>\n      \u003c/topichead>\n    \n      \u003ctopichead navtitle=\"Recording and editing\">\n   @@ -25,7 +28,7 @@\n      \u003c/topichead>\n    \n      \u003ctopichead navtitle=\"Reference\" id=\"reference\">\n   -    \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/supported-audio-formats.dita\" locktitle=\"yes\">\n   +    \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/supported-audio-formats.dita\" keys=\"formats\" locktitle=\"yes\">\n          \u003ctopicmeta>\n            \u003cnavtitle>Audio formats\u003c/navtitle>\n          \u003c/topicmeta>\n   ```\n2. **Read the map**\n\n   - `\u003cmapref href=\"keydefs-product.ditamap\"/>` includes another map. Its key definitions join the guide's key space; a `\u003ckeydef>` that is not reachable from the root map defines nothing.\n   - `\u003ckeydef keys=\"start-here\" href=\"topics/what-is-audacity.dita\"/>` gives a topic a key without adding it to the table of contents: a keydef is `@processing-role=\"resource-only\"` by default.\n   - `@keys` on a `\u003ctopicref>` that is already in the guide, such as `keys=\"install\"`, keys the topic in place. The key space is `start-here`, `digital-audio`, `install`, `formats` and the four product keys.\n:::\n\n## Step 3: Use the keys in the topics {#step-3-use-the-keys-in-the-topics}\n\n:::steps\n1. **Edit the topics** Every literal \"Audacity\" becomes `\u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/>`, the install task gains the version and the download link, and three links go through keys.\n\n   ```diff {title=\"topics/installing-audacity.dita\"}\n   --- a/topics/installing-audacity.dita\n   +++ b/topics/installing-audacity.dita\n   @@ -2,19 +2,19 @@\n    \u003c!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN\" \"task.dtd\">\n    \n    \u003ctask id=\"installing-audacity\">\n   -  \u003ctitle>Installing Audacity\u003c/title>\n   -  \u003cshortdesc>Download Audacity from the official website, or install it with your package manager, and launch it once to finish set