      <h1 id="stage-10-keys" class="group scroll-mt-20">Stage 10: Keys<a href="#stage-10-keys" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h1>
      <p>Define keys for the product name, version, download URL, and selected topics. A <code>&lt;keyword keyref="product-name"/&gt;</code> uses text from a key definition; an <code>&lt;xref keyref="install"/&gt;</code> uses a key to identify a link target. Updating the definition changes each reference that resolves to it.</p>
      <p>Store product values in <code>keydefs-product.ditamap</code> and include that map with <code>&lt;mapref&gt;</code>. Define topic keys with <code>@keys</code> on the guide's existing <code>&lt;topicref&gt;</code> elements.</p>
      <p><strong>Time:</strong> about 30 minutes. <strong>You need:</strong> stage 09 complete.</p>
      <p>Recorded diagnostic examples below come from earlier runs. File counts, paths, and stage numbers can differ. Run the gate for your current checkout.</p>
      <h2 id="step-1-define-the-product-keys" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 1: Define the product keys<a href="#step-1-define-the-product-keys" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Create </strong><strong><code>keydefs-product.ditamap</code></strong> in the project root.
      <CodeBlock code={"\u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n\u003c!DOCTYPE map PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Map//EN\" \"map.dtd\">\n\n\u003cmap>\n  \u003ctitle>Product key definitions\u003c/title>\n\n  \u003ckeydef keys=\"product-name\">\n    \u003ctopicmeta>\n      \u003ckeywords>\n        \u003ckeyword>Audacity\u003c/keyword>\n      \u003c/keywords>\n    \u003c/topicmeta>\n  \u003c/keydef>\n  \u003ckeydef keys=\"product-version\">\n    \u003ctopicmeta>\n      \u003ckeywords>\n        \u003ckeyword>3.4\u003c/keyword>\n      \u003c/keywords>\n    \u003c/topicmeta>\n  \u003c/keydef>\n  \u003ckeydef keys=\"download-url\" href=\"https://www.audacityteam.org/download/\" scope=\"external\" format=\"html\">\n    \u003ctopicmeta>\n      \u003clinktext>the Audacity download page\u003c/linktext>\n    \u003c/topicmeta>\n  \u003c/keydef>\n  \u003ckeydef keys=\"project-extension\">\n    \u003ctopicmeta>\n      \u003ckeywords>\n        \u003ckeyword>.aup3\u003c/keyword>\n      \u003c/keywords>\n    \u003c/topicmeta>\n  \u003c/keydef>\n\u003c/map>"} lang="xml" title="keydefs-product.ditamap" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the elements</strong>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;keydef&gt;</code> is a <code>&lt;topicref&gt;</code> specialized for defining keys. <code>@keys</code> is the key name. A <code>&lt;keydef&gt;</code> with no <code>@href</code> defines text only.</li>
      <li>The text comes from <code>&lt;keywords&gt;</code> inside <code>&lt;topicmeta&gt;</code>: the <code>&lt;keyword&gt;</code> is what a <code>&lt;keyword keyref&gt;</code> in a topic renders as.</li>
      <li><code>download-url</code> has an <code>@href</code> with <code>@scope="external"</code> and <code>@format="html"</code>, exactly as an external <code>&lt;xref&gt;</code> in stage 07. Its <code>&lt;linktext&gt;</code> is the text an empty <code>&lt;xref keyref="download-url"/&gt;</code> shows, because a web page has no DITA title to borrow.</li>
      <li>A keydef map is an ordinary map with a <code>&lt;title&gt;</code>. It is never published on its own; the guide references it.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-2-bring-the-keys-into-the-guide-and-key-the-topics" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 2: Bring the keys into the guide and key the topics<a href="#step-2-bring-the-keys-into-the-guide-and-key-the-topics" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><strong><code>audacity-guide.ditamap</code></strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/audacity-guide.ditamap\n+++ b/audacity-guide.ditamap\n@@ -7,11 +7,14 @@\n     \u003cshortdesc>Record, edit and export audio with Audacity, from your first track to a finished file.\u003c/shortdesc>\n   \u003c/topicmeta>\n \n+  \u003cmapref href=\"keydefs-product.ditamap\"/>\n+  \u003ckeydef keys=\"start-here\" href=\"topics/what-is-audacity.dita\"/>\n+\n   \u003ctopichead navtitle=\"Getting started\">\n     \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/what-is-audacity.dita\" collection-type=\"family\">\n-      \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\"/>\n+      \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\" keys=\"digital-audio\"/>\n     \u003c/topicref>\n-    \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/installing-audacity.dita\"/>\n+    \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/installing-audacity.dita\" keys=\"install\"/>\n   \u003c/topichead>\n \n   \u003ctopichead navtitle=\"Recording and editing\">\n@@ -25,7 +28,7 @@\n   \u003c/topichead>\n \n   \u003ctopichead navtitle=\"Reference\" id=\"reference\">\n-    \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/supported-audio-formats.dita\" locktitle=\"yes\">\n+    \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/supported-audio-formats.dita\" keys=\"formats\" locktitle=\"yes\">\n       \u003ctopicmeta>\n         \u003cnavtitle>Audio formats\u003c/navtitle>\n       \u003c/topicmeta>"} lang="diff" title="audacity-guide.ditamap" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the map</strong>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;mapref href="keydefs-product.ditamap"/&gt;</code> includes another map. Its key definitions join the guide's key space; a <code>&lt;keydef&gt;</code> that is not reachable from the root map defines nothing.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;keydef keys="start-here" href="topics/what-is-audacity.dita"/&gt;</code> gives a topic a key without adding it to the table of contents: a keydef is <code>@processing-role="resource-only"</code> by default.</li>
      <li><code>@keys</code> on a <code>&lt;topicref&gt;</code> that is already in the guide, such as <code>keys="install"</code>, keys the topic in place. The key space is <code>start-here</code>, <code>digital-audio</code>, <code>install</code>, <code>formats</code> and the four product keys.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-3-use-the-keys-in-the-topics" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 3: Use the keys in the topics<a href="#step-3-use-the-keys-in-the-topics" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit the topics</strong> Every literal "Audacity" becomes <code>&lt;keyword keyref="product-name"/&gt;</code>, the install task gains the version and the download link, and three links go through keys.
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/installing-audacity.dita\n+++ b/topics/installing-audacity.dita\n@@ -2,19 +2,19 @@\n \u003c!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN\" \"task.dtd\">\n \n \u003ctask id=\"installing-audacity\">\n-  \u003ctitle>Installing Audacity\u003c/title>\n-  \u003cshortdesc>Download Audacity from the official website, or install it with your package manager, and launch it once to finish setup.\u003c/shortdesc>\n+  \u003ctitle>Installing \u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/>\u003c/title>\n+  \u003cshortdesc>Download \u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> from the official website, or install it with your package manager, and launch it once to finish setup.\u003c/shortdesc>\n   \u003ctaskbody>\n     \u003cprereq>\n       \u003cp>You need about 250 MB of free disk space and an account that can install software.\u003c/p>\n     \u003c/prereq>\n     \u003ccontext>\n-      \u003cp>Audacity is available for Windows, macOS and Linux.\n+      \u003cp>\u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> is available for Windows, macOS and Linux.\n       The steps differ by operating system only at the install step.\u003c/p>\n     \u003c/context>\n     \u003csteps>\n       \u003cstep>\n-        \u003ccmd>Download Audacity from \u003cfilepath>https://www.audacityteam.org/download/\u003c/filepath>.\u003c/cmd>\n+        \u003ccmd>Download \u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> \u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-version\"/> from \u003cxref keyref=\"download-url\"/>.\u003c/cmd>\n         \u003cinfo>\n           \u003cp>Select the installer for your operating system.\u003c/p>\n         \u003c/info>\n@@ -33,7 +33,7 @@\n           \u003c/chrow>\n           \u003cchrow>\n             \u003cchoption>macOS\u003c/choption>\n-            \u003cchdesc>Open the downloaded \u003cfilepath>.dmg\u003c/filepath> file and drag Audacity to your \u003cfilepath>Applications\u003c/filepath> folder.\u003c/chdesc>\n+            \u003cchdesc>Open the downloaded \u003cfilepath>.dmg\u003c/filepath> file and drag \u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> to your \u003cfilepath>Applications\u003c/filepath> folder.\u003c/chdesc>\n           \u003c/chrow>\n           \u003cchrow>\n             \u003cchoption>Linux\u003c/choption>\n@@ -42,10 +42,10 @@\n         \u003c/choicetable>\n       \u003c/step>\n       \u003cstep>\n-        \u003ccmd>Launch Audacity.\u003c/cmd>\n+        \u003ccmd>Launch \u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/>.\u003c/cmd>\n         \u003csubsteps>\n           \u003csubstep>\n-            \u003ccmd>If Audacity asks to scan for audio plugins, click \u003cuicontrol>OK\u003c/uicontrol>.\u003c/cmd>\n+            \u003ccmd>If \u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> asks to scan for audio plugins, click \u003cuicontrol>OK\u003c/uicontrol>.\u003c/cmd>\n             \u003cinfo>\n               \u003cp>This happens once, on first launch.\u003c/p>\n             \u003c/info>\n@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@\n       \u003c/step>\n     \u003c/steps>\n     \u003cresult>\n-      \u003cp>Audacity is installed and ready to use.\u003c/p>\n+      \u003cp>\u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> \u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-version\"/> is installed and ready to use.\u003c/p>\n     \u003c/result>\n     \u003cpostreq>\n       \u003cp>Connect a microphone, then continue with \u003cxref href=\"recording-your-first-track.dita\"/>.\u003c/p>"} lang="diff" title="topics/installing-audacity.dita" />
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/exporting-audio.dita\n+++ b/topics/exporting-audio.dita\n@@ -7,7 +7,7 @@\n   \u003ctaskbody>\n     \u003cprereq>\n       \u003cp>Finish editing and save the project.\n-      A project file (\u003cfilepath>.aup3\u003c/filepath>) can only be opened by Audacity; exporting creates an ordinary audio file.\u003c/p>\n+      A project file (\u003cfilepath>.aup3\u003c/filepath>) can only be opened by \u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/>; exporting creates an ordinary audio file.\u003c/p>\n     \u003c/prereq>\n     \u003csteps>\n       \u003cstep>\n@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@\n         \u003c/stepresult>\n       \u003c/step>\n       \u003cstep>\n-        \u003ccmd>Choose a format (see \u003cxref href=\"supported-audio-formats.dita#supported-audio-formats/choosing\"/>).\u003c/cmd>\n+        \u003ccmd>Choose a format (see \u003cxref keyref=\"formats/choosing\"/>).\u003c/cmd>\n         \u003cchoices>\n           \u003cchoice>Choose \u003cuicontrol>WAV\u003c/uicontrol> or \u003cuicontrol>FLAC\u003c/uicontrol> for an archive copy with no quality loss.\u003c/choice>\n           \u003cchoice>Choose \u003cuicontrol>MP3\u003c/uicontrol> or \u003cuicontrol>OGG\u003c/uicontrol> for a small file to share.\u003c/choice>"} lang="diff" title="topics/exporting-audio.dita" />
