      <Step>
      <strong>Read the four forms of reference</strong>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;keyword keyref="product-name"/&gt;</code>: variable text. The element is empty; the processor fills in the <code>&lt;keyword&gt;</code> from the keydef. It works in a <code>&lt;title&gt;</code> and a <code>&lt;shortdesc&gt;</code> as well as in a <code>&lt;p&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;xref keyref="download-url"/&gt;</code>: a link through a key to an external page. The text is the keydef's <code>&lt;linktext&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;xref keyref="formats/choosing"/&gt;</code>: a link to an element inside a keyed topic. <code>key/element-id</code> replaces <code>file#topic/element-id</code>; the topic id is not needed because the key already names the topic.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;link keyref="install"/&gt;</code>: a related link through a key, with the text taken from the target's title as before.</li>
      <li>Keep the example file name <code>&lt;filepath&gt;podcast-episode-1.aup3&lt;/filepath&gt;</code> literal. Stage 11 uses <code>project-extension</code> for the extension itself.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-4-list-the-key-space" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 4: List the key space<a href="#step-4-list-the-key-space" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Run the keys command</strong> The DogsBay XML command line resolves the key space of a root map. Pass the root map as the argument.
      <CodeBlock code={"dogsbay-xml keys audacity-guide.ditamap"} lang="bash" />
      <CodeBlock code={"start-here  →  topics/what-is-audacity.dita   [/home/you/audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:11]  file: /home/you/audacity-guide/topics/what-is-audacity.dita\ndigital-audio  →  topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita   [/home/you/audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:15]  file: /home/you/audacity-guide/topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\ninstall  →  topics/installing-audacity.dita   [/home/you/audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:17]  file: /home/you/audacity-guide/topics/installing-audacity.dita\nformats  →  topics/supported-audio-formats.dita   [/home/you/audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:31]  file: /home/you/audacity-guide/topics/supported-audio-formats.dita\nproduct-name  →  \"Audacity\"   [/home/you/audacity-guide/keydefs-product.ditamap:7]\nproduct-version  →  \"3.4\"   [/home/you/audacity-guide/keydefs-product.ditamap:14]\ndownload-url  →  \"the Audacity download page\"   [/home/you/audacity-guide/keydefs-product.ditamap:21]\nproject-extension  →  \".aup3\"   [/home/you/audacity-guide/keydefs-product.ditamap:26]\n8 key(s)."} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>A topic key shows the file it resolves to; a text key shows its text; each shows the map and line that defines it. Keys from the <code>&lt;mapref&gt;</code> are listed as part of the guide's key space.</p>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-5-update-the-readme-and-run-the-gate" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 5: Update the README and run the gate<a href="#step-5-update-the-readme-and-run-the-gate" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Change the "You are on" line and the layout</strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@\n \n Build a guide through 27 stages. Maps begin at stage 02; HTML publication begins at stage 03.\n \n-You are on stage 09: map structure.\n+You are on stage 10: keys.\n \n ## Stages\n "} lang="diff" title="README.md" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Format and check</strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"dogsbay-xml format -i topics/*.dita\nscripts/check-stage.sh"} lang="bash" />
      <CodeBlock code={"== validate-project  /home/you/audacity-guide ==\n11 file(s): 11 valid, 0 invalid.\n\n== project-health  /home/you/audacity-guide ==\nRoot map: audacity-guide.ditamap (project config); house rules: none (none configured)\nProject is healthy: valid, no broken references, keys, orphans, or broken element ids.\n\n== build  project.json -> /tmp/check-stage-357688 ==\nall deliverables built\n\nSTAGE OK"} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>Run <code>dita --project=project.json</code> to build in the project directory. Open <code>out/full/topics/installing-audacity.html</code>: the title reads <em>Installing Audacity</em>, the download step reads "Download Audacity 3.4 from the Audacity download page" with the link on the last five words, after DITA-OT resolves the key references.</p>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <p>Test an undefined key reference. Change both occurrences of <code>keyref="product-version"</code> in the install task to <code>product-verson</code> and run the gate:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"== project-health  /home/you/audacity-guide ==\nRoot map: audacity-guide.ditamap (project config); house rules: none (none configured)\nUndefined keys (2):\n  /home/you/audacity-guide/topics/installing-audacity.dita:17  key 'product-verson' not defined\n  /home/you/audacity-guide/topics/installing-audacity.dita:63  key 'product-verson' not defined\nUnused keys (4):\n  start-here  [/home/you/audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:11]\n  digital-audio  [/home/you/audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:15]\n  product-version  [/home/you/audacity-guide/keydefs-product.ditamap:14]\n  project-extension  [/home/you/audacity-guide/keydefs-product.ditamap:26]\n\nSummary\n  Undefined keys                2\n  Unused keys                   4\nFAIL: project-health found issues"} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>The file validates, since <code>@keyref</code> is only a name to the DTD, and DITA-OT would build the page with the version missing. The <em>Unused keys</em> list provides diagnostic information: <code>start-here</code>, <code>digital-audio</code> and <code>project-extension</code> are defined for later stages, and the report shows them only when something else is wrong.</p>
      <h2 id="what-you-learned" class="group scroll-mt-20">What you learned<a href="#what-you-learned" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;keydef keys="…"&gt;</code> with <code>&lt;keywords&gt;</code>/<code>&lt;keyword&gt;</code> defines variable text; with <code>@href</code> it defines a link target, and <code>&lt;linktext&gt;</code> names an external one.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;mapref&gt;</code> includes a map, keys and all; <code>@keys</code> on a <code>&lt;topicref&gt;</code> keys a topic in place; a <code>&lt;keydef&gt;</code> is resource-only and stays out of the table of contents.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;keyword keyref&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;xref keyref&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;link keyref&gt;</code>, and <code>key/element-id</code> for an element inside a keyed topic.</li>
      <li><code>dogsbay-xml keys &lt;rootmap&gt;</code> lists the key space; <code>project-health</code> reports undefined keys.</li>
      </ul>
